# Local development — point the Next.js proxy to the local .NET backend.
# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored) and keep the value below unless
# your backend runs on a different port.
#
# Without this, the API proxy in src/app/api/[...proxy]/route.ts falls back
# to the live production backend. That backend runs in the Production ASP.NET
# environment, which sets auth cookies with `Secure; SameSite=None` — cookies
# a plain http://localhost frontend cannot store. Symptom: registration/login
# requests appear to succeed (200 OK) but you get silently bounced back to
# the login page and can never reach the dashboard.
BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:5165
